Hi all,

This week at D-RUG we’ll have guest speaker Carl Boettiger <http://www.carlboettiger.info/>, co-founder of ROpenSci <http://ropensci.org/>. ROpenSci develops R packages that provide access to a variety of online scientific data repositories <http://ropensci.org/packages/index.html#data_access>, full-text journal articles, and data on scholarly metrics so you can download and analyze these within R. Carl will talk about some of these packages and walk through how to use them to retrieve, process, and upload data.

Per usual, we’ll be in Wickson 2124. Carl will speak 10-11 and we’ll have open work time 11-12, with Carl around to answer questions.

For a preview, try out these quick examples of what some ROpenSci packages can do:

Get and map all the observations of a species from the Berkeley Natural History Museum’s EcoEngine database:
install.packages("ecoengine"); library(ecoengine)
Artemisia <- ee_observations(scientific_name = "Artemisia douglasiana")
ee_map(Artemisia)

Search across PloS journals:
install.packages('rplos'); library(rplos)
searchplos('Phytophthora ramorum', c('id','title'), limit = 10)
`

Get all species in a taxon from the Catalogue of Life
install.packages("taxize); library(taxize)
downstream("Apis", downto = "Species", db = "col")
​

